# What never reaches Vercel.
#
# This file carries ALL of the exclusions. vercel.json's `excludeFiles` cannot:
# it is capped at 256 characters, and the list below is far longer than that.
# .vercelignore has no length limit and excludes files from the upload itself,
# which is strictly better - an excluded file is never transferred, never
# builds, and never counts toward the function bundle.
#
# The two files the model needs are NOT listed here, and are pulled into the
# function bundle explicitly by `includeFiles` in vercel.json:
#   models/blaze_face_short_range.tflite
#   runs/improved_resnet18/best_model.pt
#
# Note: frontend/ sources are deliberately NOT excluded. The build command
# compiles them on Vercel, so removing them here would break the build.

.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Datasets and derived artifacts. Training-only, and enormous.
data/
processed/
artifacts/

frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/

# Training experiments. The SERVED checkpoint lives in runs/improved_resnet18/
# and is kept; everything else under runs/ is experiment history.
runs/exp*/
runs/phase*/
runs/comparison/
runs/baseline_resnet18/
runs/**/*.csv
runs/**/*.log

# Training and analysis scripts - never imported by backend/app/main.py
train_*.py
preprocess*.py
prepare_expw.py
merge_datasets.py
domain_probe.py
provenance_aug.py
compare_models.py
verify_checkpoint.py
verify_setup.py
phase4*.py
video_pipeline.py
setup.bat
docs/
